  "id": "Compound::DB00796 - Disease::DOID:10763",
  "verbalization": "Candesartan is supported by multiple pathways to the disease hypertension, primarily through its resemblance to other angiotensin II receptor antagonists. The shared structural features with Azilsartan Medoxomil and Telmisartan, which in turn treat hypertension, suggest a potential mechanism of action involving the angiotensin II receptor. This connection is reinforced by the common ancestor relationship between Candesartan and these compounds, which are all classified under the broader category of angiotensin II receptor antagonists. The evidence also highlights a recurring link between Candesartan and the angiotensin II receptor pathway, which is a well-established target for antihypertensive drugs. The similarity in molecular structure and the downstream effect on hypertension support the hypothesis that Candesartan may have a similar therapeutic profile to its structural relatives, potentially making it a candidate for repositioning in the treatment of hypertension.",
